{
 "edition": "daily-2026-11-12",
 "date": "2026-11-12",
 "url": "issues/daily/2026/11/2026-11-12.html",
 "subject": "Google brings Gemini 4 to everyone at a lower price",
 "body": "<!-- buttondown-editor-mode: fancy -->\n<div style=\"display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;mso-hide:all\">Also: OpenAI&#x27;s agents fix security holes, Claude joins video calls, Anthropic&#x27;s agents run in-house, Copilot drops its agent picker, and Meta&#x27;s agent makes calls.</div>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Thursday, November 12, 2026 · <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/issues/daily/2026/11/2026-11-12.html\">Read on the web</a></p>\n<h1 style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:28px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:#111111\">Google brings Gemini 4 to everyone at a lower price</h1>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">Also: OpenAI's agents fix security holes, Claude joins video calls, Anthropic's agents run in-house, Copilot drops its agent picker, and Meta's agent makes calls.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">What matters today</h2>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-12-0.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Gemini 4 Hydrogen release art\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/introducing-gemini-4-hydrogen/\">Google</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Gemini 4 for everyone</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/introducing-gemini-4-hydrogen/\">Google releases Gemini 4 Hydrogen, its fast everyday model</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Price:</strong> $1.50 in and $7.50 out per million tokens, flat across a 1 million token window. Google's figures: <strong>51 against 50</strong> for Gemini 4 Argon on an independent index.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Available now</strong> in Search worldwide, the Gemini app, the API and AI Studio. In Antigravity, <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://antigravity.google/blog/gemini-4-hydrogen-in-google-antigravity/\">Orchestrator</a> hands steps between Carbon and Hydrogen, using 24% less quota.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>The cheap model now scores like the top one. Most of a product's AI work can run on it, with the costly model kept for the hard steps, so features get cheaper without getting worse.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-12-1.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Agents that attack and fix</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/daybreak/red-team/\">OpenAI launches agents that test web apps for security holes</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Red Team, early access:</strong> several agents read an app's code and context, probe attack paths and confirm real flaws, inside isolated environments with limits on what they can reach.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Defense Factory, preview in ChatGPT:</strong> agents trace each flaw and <strong>draft the fix as a pull request</strong> for engineers to review. It also takes findings from Wiz and Snyk.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Finding a flaw and fixing it become one job for the same agents. Security work shifts from a report someone files to a pull request someone approves, and tools get judged on fixes, not findings.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-12-2.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Claude on a video call building a shared event plan on a whiteboard\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://claude.com/resources/articles/claude-meetings\">Anthropic</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Claude joins the call</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://claude.com/resources/articles/claude-meetings\">Anthropic puts Claude into video calls as a participant</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>During the call:</strong> answers questions, <strong>builds docs and whiteboards</strong> teammates edit live, and writes notes and action items. It uses each person's connected tools with their permission.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>In beta</strong> on Team and Enterprise plans, starting with Google Meet. It stays out of calls with outside guests unless an admin allows it.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>The meeting becomes a place where work gets made, not just recorded. Meeting apps now compete with the assistant people already use, which leaves with a draft plan, not a transcript.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-12-3.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Anthropic illustration of a keyhole on a laptop screen\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://claude.com/resources/articles/self-hosted-claude-managed-agents\">Anthropic</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Agents behind your firewall</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://claude.com/resources/articles/self-hosted-claude-managed-agents\">Anthropic lets companies run its whole agent service themselves</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Private beta:</strong> the agent loop, sandboxes, keys and history run in a company's own cloud or data center. Claude calls go to Anthropic, a cloud provider or the company's gateway.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Built-in limits:</strong> passwords and keys stay outside the sandbox, each agent can reach <strong>only listed hosts</strong>, and every step is logged for existing monitoring tools.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Agent software is becoming something a company installs, like a database, not rents. Anthropic still sells the model while the customer keeps the data and logs, a common reason to say no.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-12-4.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">One chat, no agent picker</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://mc.merill.net/message/MC1550540\">Microsoft drops the agent picker in Copilot Workspaces</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Agentic chat:</strong> users describe the task and Copilot applies research, analysis or design skills itself, instead of people choosing <strong>Researcher, Analyst or Designer</strong>.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Frontier preview</strong> from December 2026. The three agents stay in the Microsoft 365 Copilot app. Copilot Workspaces was called Copilot Notebooks.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>People should not have to know which agent does what. Named agents are turning into skills behind one chat box, and products that ask users to pick an agent first will start to feel dated.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-12-5.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">An agent that makes calls</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/12/muse-can-now-place-calls-to-u-s-businesses-if-you-pay/\">Meta's Muse now phones businesses for its users</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Available now</strong> to paid US subscribers: Muse calls a cable company, an insurer or a restaurant that takes no online bookings. Free users cannot use it.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Price:</strong> plans start at <strong>$20 a month</strong> for 500 million Muse tokens a week. Gemini and the startup Instinct already offer similar calling.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>The phone line becomes another place agents do work for people. Any business that serves customers by phone now has callers that are agents, and has to decide whether to serve them or block them.</p></div>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Research worth watching</h2>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://alignment.anthropic.com/2026/worse-together\">Agents do worse sharing a job</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">When each person sent their own agent to a shared task, like a group order or a shared budget, <strong>results were worse in all four tests</strong> than one agent serving everyone. A named leader and clear priorities helped.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Products where many users' agents meet need a referee, not just more agents.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/11/12/trained-to-betray-how-post-training-supply-chain-attacks-hijack-coding-agents/\">A poisoned model turns on its user</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">Microsoft hid a backdoor in open-weight coding models: an ordinary request made the agent misuse its command tools. <strong>It worked 84% to 95% of the time</strong> on code the model had never seen.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Where a fine-tuned model came from now matters as much as how it scores.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2608.22237\">Agents read far less, lose nothing</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">SparseRead shows an agent only the parts of pages and tool results it needs. <strong>Tokens fell by up to 93%</strong> and run time by up to 89%, with quality kept or improved in 97% of settings.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Much of an agent's bill is reading it never needed to do.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.13410\">Shrink an agent, keep its skill</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">SteerDistill has the full model coach a compressed copy where it fails. The 4-bit agent <strong>stays within one point</strong> of the full model on five agent tests, with 67% fewer training hours than a rival method.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Cheap, compressed agents no longer have to mean weaker ones.</p></div>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Community signal</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50471731\">Microsoft 365 outage</a>: mailboxes and other services were down for whole organizations in the Americas, and the status page itself barely loaded. 930 points, 804 comments.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50474883\">Chips in Chinese models</a>: a report says the weights of six Chinese models show traces of Nvidia Blackwell chips that cannot be exported to China; commenters called export rules friction, not a barrier. 304 points, 110 comments.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50463899\">Vibe coding at Humble Bundle</a>: users said a rebuilt site let them sign in without two-factor codes, and argued whether to blame the AI or the people using it. 384 points, 228 comments.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Top launches yesterday</h2>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/e87131be-1490-4ed2-a291-5f91da603996.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://simulation.plurai.ai/connect\">Plurai Simulation</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">A simulated copy of an agent's world, with fake users, documents and tools, to find failures before real users do.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/f47c5780-5a8a-4458-90ed-2700c2f4d548.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://youart.ai/\">YouArt Desktop App</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">A creative assistant on your computer that gathers files and context and runs apps such as After Effects and Blender.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/7dc98c53-4374-466e-97f8-388ca136aad3.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://omnigraph.dev/\">Omnigraph</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">An open-source graph database that gives agents one shared knowledge base, with changes reviewed before they merge.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/7afdfaf6-038f-411e-ae40-484f9355f96a.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://letter.dev/commandl\">⌘+L</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Edit a live website visually, like a design file, and a coding agent turns the edits into a pull request.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/74983efe-60a0-4e2f-b04f-bbf40437df85.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://spacefast.com/\">Spacefast by Automattic</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Ask ChatGPT, Claude or Cursor to publish a site or app, with hosting, database and domain handled.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/a5c5c624-3bdc-4d2a-998e-20e4f8ef8f4d.jpeg?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://www.adobe.com/ai/overview/ai-assistant\">Adobe AI Assistant</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Describe a creative goal and it carries out steps across Photoshop, Premiere, Illustrator and other Adobe apps, for you to approve.</div></td></tr></table>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Also in AI today</h2>\n<ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://mc.merill.net/message/MC1550533\"><strong>Copilot scheduled tasks</strong></a>: move off Power Platform to Copilot's own scheduling, up to 10 active per user; worldwide from November 30; the old version retires December 31.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://mc.merill.net/message/MC1409304\"><strong>Teams Facilitator</strong></a>: the meeting agent that answers unanswered factual questions in chat slips to February 2027 (was December); needs Microsoft 365 Copilot.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://claude.com/resources/articles/claude-for-manufacturing\"><strong>Claude for Manufacturing</strong></a>: a plugin with 17 skills, from quotes to breakdowns, and connectors to Autodesk Fusion, Infor, Microsoft 365 and NetSuite; Team and Enterprise plans.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/children-first-declaration\"><strong>OpenAI on children's safety</strong></a>: $2 million for research and shared tools to measure AI's risks and benefits for young people.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.databricks.com/blog/genie-slack-now-generally-available-governed-ai-cowork-right-where-work-happens\"><strong>Genie in Slack</strong></a>: generally available; answers in channels and DMs with each asker's data permissions, and updates documents and tickets after approval.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://devin.ai/blog/devin-teams-plan\"><strong>Devin Teams</strong></a>: every user gets Devin Desktop and two free concurrent sessions on Cognition's own SWE-2 model; admins get single sign-on and cost controls.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/11/cognito-token-exchange/\"><strong>Amazon Cognito</strong></a>: an agent acting for a user can swap the user's token for a narrower one that records the agent as the actor; all regions.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://kiro.dev/blog/android\"><strong>Kiro for Android</strong></a>: start, steer and review cloud coding sessions from a phone, then open the pull request; paid plans.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/xr-ar/google-intelligent-eyewear-collections-pre-order/\"><strong>Google intelligent eyewear</strong></a>: Gemini glasses from Warby Parker and Gentle Monster open for pre-order, <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://arstechnica.com/google/2026/11/google-pushes-privacy-angle-as-gemini-powered-smartglasses-debut-starting-at-395/\">from $395</a>; in stores December 10.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://pandaily.com/bytedance-seedance-2-5-flash-faster-lower-cost-video-model-volcano-ark-api\"><strong>Seedance 2.5 Flash</strong></a>: ByteDance's video model runs twice as fast as Seedance 2.5 at about 34% lower price; API from November 15.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://hark.com/articles/introducing-hark-handoff-now-2x-faster\"><strong>Hark Handoff²</strong></a>: its agent that uses websites for you now finishes tasks twice as fast; 82% of Hark's test tasks done, up from 73%; all Hark Pro plans.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://pandaily.com/tencent-yuanbao-search-standalone-ai-search-so-qq-com\"><strong>Yuanbao Search</strong></a>: Tencent launches a separate AI search product that answers over the web, WeChat articles and papers, with cited sources.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/article/anthropic-ipo-claude-maker-to-begin-trading-on-thursday-nov-19-173550865.html\"><strong>Anthropic IPO</strong></a>: shares to be priced November 18 and to start trading November 19 under ANT.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.salesforce.com/blog/artex-agentic-ai-attacks/\"><strong>ARTEX attacks</strong></a>: Salesforce sees several groups using this open-source attack agent against customers through stolen app credentials; no platform flaw.</li></ul>\n<hr style=\"border:0;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;margin:32px 0 16px\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">You get the AI Brief because you subscribed at <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/\">ai.mediancanadian.ca</a>. <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"{{ unsubscribe_url }}\">Unsubscribe</a> at any time; it takes effect at once.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;